{"kind":"artifact","text":"The fold projects the satisfier it bound at admission, so a reader can tell who may ratify a record without replaying the kind definitions itself. Exact clean pushed head 8ad3c0c20b6d374b036f3e4b3dd86ef0ad4f8627 on request/decision-records-ui-recut; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash 1f7e7907, checkout clean. Successor to 90f43d2b, republished at the corrected head and with an error of mine fixed.\n\nWHAT THIS PATH CHANGES, unchanged in substance from the predecessor. fold.go adds a Satisfier field projected per statement from the definition captured on the record at admission, and schema.go advances the profile to workroom-fold@13 so a cache written under @12 is rejected and the history replayed. Without that gate a cache predating the field would answer every reader \"no satisfier\", and every ratification would be silently withheld from actors entitled to make it. The two goldens take insertion-only additions, 10 added satisfier lines and zero deletions. Nothing at this path changed between f6489c78a and this head; it is republished so the artifact set names one exact head.\n\nTHE CORRECTION, WHICH IS MINE. 90f43d2b said fold_test.go \"adds the departed-author regression and the migration witness\". That misstated where two of the three tests live, and codex was right to flag it at P3 in 22db9df6. Accurately: internal/workroom/fold_test.go adds the admitted-time satisfier regression. The departed-requester UI regression is in ui/test/before-signing.test.mjs. The cache migration witness from @12 to @13 is in internal/app/app_test.go. Each sits in the package that owns the behaviour it pins, which is the right arrangement; my sentence simply claimed all three for this path. A reviewer reading that artifact to find the tests would have looked in the wrong file, which is the whole cost of the error and the reason it is worth a correction rather than a silent republish.\n\nWHY THE PROJECTION IS NECESSARY RATHER THAN CONVENIENT. The captured definition is not in the projection, so the value is not recoverable from what a reader is given: reconstructing it would mean replaying every kind definition and its ratifications in reading order, which is this layer's authority rule rebuilt outside this layer. An empty satisfier means the fold bound no definition and nothing may be ratified on it. I re-checked that decideRatify reads target.definition.Satisfier, the same captured definition, so the projection publishes exactly what the fold decides on.\n\nCARRY SAFETY. Nothing at this path was touched by main's three intervening merges, so no landed fix can be reverted by this carry.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD. gofmt -l . empty; go build ./... and go vet ./... exit 0 with no output; go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 32 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 33 packages, zero failures and zero cached; npm test --prefix ui 99 tests, 99 pass, 0 fail; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"8ad3c0c20b6d374b036f3e4b3dd86ef0ad4f8627","path":"internal/workroom"}}